# Excalidraw Architecture

## State Management

- Custom state via actionManager - NOT Redux/Zustand/MobX
- State updates: actionManager.dispatch() ONLY
- State type: AppState (packages/excalidraw/types.ts)

## Rendering

- Canvas 2D rendering - NOT React DOM for drawing
- Render pipeline: Scene -> renderScene() -> canvas context
- DO NOT use react-konva, fabric.js, pixi.js

## Dependencies

- No new npm packages without explicit approval
- Check packages/utils/ before adding external helpers

## How to verify

- Search changed files for forbidden state libs: `Redux`, `Zustand`, `MobX`, `jotai` imports used as editor state (Jotai helpers must follow existing wrapper rules).
- Confirm updates to scene/editor state go through `actionManager.dispatch()` patterns, not ad-hoc global stores.
- Ensure canvas work stays in the existing render pipeline; grep for disallowed render libs (`react-konva`, `fabric`, `pixi`) only if rendering approach changes.
